@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il06-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il06-period`

-- ===========================================================================================
-- Basic amounts for the child allowance PUBLISHED BY THE NATIONAL INSURANCE INSTITUTE.
-- NOT ENCODED LAW.
--
-- The law's figure for a basic amount on a day is the s 1 paragraph (2) amount (150, 188 or
-- 140) as updated each 1 January under s 1's updating clause, which this row does not encode
-- (row IL-04). The rules in nii-s68-amount.l4 therefore take the amounts as an input. This
-- module records what the Institute has published, so that tests and callers can use a
-- sourced figure rather than an invented one.
--
-- [nii-basic] "the basic amount for computing benefits", a page of the Institute's Research
--   and Planning site, fetched directly on 2026-10-06 14:10 UTC. Its title:
-- ext:[nii-basic] | הסכום הבסיסי לחישוב קצבאות
--     https://www.btl.gov.il/Mediniyut/GeneralData/Pages/%D7%94%D7%A1%D7%9B%D7%95%D7%9D%20%D7%94%D7%91%D7%A1%D7%99%D7%A1%D7%99%20%D7%9C%D7%97%D7%99%D7%A9%D7%95%D7%91%20%D7%A7%D7%A6%D7%91%D7%90%D7%95%D7%AA.aspx
--     193,110 bytes, sha256 d19985509135d947b3c34c0c1c462913adeddf5c9c86509ff4fccf2810994139
--   Its table has, for each date "from the day", a column "basic amount 2, for updating the
--   child allowance and the pension point in Income Support", split three ways — the three
--   limbs of s 1 paragraph (2). Its headings, as extracted from the page's HTML:
-- ext:[nii-basic] | החל ביום
-- ext:[nii-basic] | סכום בסיסי 2 לעדכון קצבת ילדים ונקודת קצבה בהבטחת הכנסה. (ש"ח)
-- ext:[nii-basic] | בעד הילד הראשון, החמישי ואילך
-- ext:[nii-basic] | בעד הילד השני, השלישי והרביעי
-- ext:[nii-basic] | לעניין גמלה לפי חוק הבטחת הכנסה
--   and its rows (shekels):
--     1.01.2026  173  219  162        1.01.2021  152  192  142
--     1.01.2025  169  214  158        1.01.2020  152  192  142
--     1.01.2024  169  214  158        1.01.2019  152  191  142
--     1.01.2023  164  207  153        1.01.2018  150  189  140
--     1.01.2022  156  197  145        1.05.2015  150  188  140
--   Rows before 1.05.2015 give a single child-allowance amount (the text before the 5776 Law)
--   and are not used. A row is read as applying from its date until the next row's date
--   (NOTES.md, assumption A3): there is no row for 2016 or 2017.
--
-- The Institute's figures are its statement, not the text of the Law. They agree with the
-- consolidation's notes on lines 187-189 for 2024-2026, and the 2025 row equals the 2024 row
-- as the updating clause's 2025 freeze (line 197) requires.
-- ===========================================================================================

§ `Basic amounts for the child allowance published by the National Insurance Institute — not encoded law`

@ref National Insurance Law s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי", updating clause (3) (source line 197): the amounts are updated on 1 January of each year; [nii-basic] has no row from 1 January 2027
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the basic amounts for the child allowance from 1 January 2027 had not been published when this model's sources were fetched` MEANS
    REFUSE "the basic amounts for the child allowance from 1 January 2027 had not been published when this model's sources were fetched"

-- One row per date of [nii-basic], newest first. Positional OF: the columns are the three
-- limbs of s 1 paragraph (2), in the order the record declares them.
@ref [nii-basic], fetched 2026-10-06, sha256 d19985509135d947b3c34c0c1c462913adeddf5c9c86509ff4fccf2810994139
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE  @desc the day asked about
GIVETH A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` `the day` MEANS
    --                                                                   (2)(a)  (2)(b)  (2)(c)
    BRANCH IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2027 1 1)
           THEN `the basic amounts for the child allowance from 1 January 2027 had not been published when this model's sources were fetched`
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2026 1 1) THEN `The basic amounts for the child allowance` OF 173, 219, 162
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2025 1 1) THEN `The basic amounts for the child allowance` OF 169, 214, 158
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2024 1 1) THEN `The basic amounts for the child allowance` OF 169, 214, 158
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2023 1 1) THEN `The basic amounts for the child allowance` OF 164, 207, 153
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2022 1 1) THEN `The basic amounts for the child allowance` OF 156, 197, 145
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2021 1 1) THEN `The basic amounts for the child allowance` OF 152, 192, 142
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2020 1 1) THEN `The basic amounts for the child allowance` OF 152, 192, 142
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2019 1 1) THEN `The basic amounts for the child allowance` OF 152, 191, 142
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2018 1 1) THEN `The basic amounts for the child allowance` OF 150, 189, 140
           IF `the day` AT LEAST (YMD 2015 5 1) THEN `The basic amounts for the child allowance` OF 150, 188, 140
           OTHERWISE `this model answers days from 1 May 2015, when sections 1 and 68 took their present wording; the text in force before then is not in its sources`
